FavoriteStorePersistenceAssembler ..> FavoriteStorePersistenceEntity
note bottom of ShoppingListCommandServiceImpl
 Creation from template: one fresh selected offer per product, same currency/compatible units.
 Do not copy old prices, budget, memberships or purchased flags.
 Unique owner/creation-key; retry with same semantic input returns original id.
 Check ownership before returning an idempotent result; mismatch -> conflict.
 All item mutations require ACTIVE and expected version; completion is explicit.
end note
note bottom of ShoppingReferenceProvider
 Contract only; trusted Catalog/store provisioning and freshness rules remain pending.
 No ACL or implemented cross-context client is implied.
 Required reference unavailable -> 503; never invent a current price or availability.
end note
note bottom of BudgetStatusView
 US11: warning = budget exists AND projectedTotal > limit.
 Recompute on every query; clear at or below limit. No warning event.
end note
note bottom of PurchaseProgressView
 Checkout includes only purchased items; unmarking reduces it.
 Template clones start with zero purchased items and zero checkout total.
end note
note bottom of FavoriteStoreRepositoryImpl
 Atomic unique identity and optimistic version prevent duplicate active preferences.
 Unchanged operations publish nothing; changed aggregates use PublishAndClearEvents after save.
 Only PersistenceEntity classes carry JPA; no durable event-delivery guarantee.
end note
@enduml
